  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 203.05 Scheduling of Hearing. Unless otherwise provided in these rules, each hearing shall be assigned a hearing number and set for a date as soon as practical after the complaint has been received and reviewed. The hearing shall be scheduled to allow a reasonable time for preparation of the case by both the department and the parties.\n\nSource. #2250, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2946-a, eff 1-3-85; ss by #4451, eff 6-24-88; ss by #4844, eff 6-20-90; ss by #6249, INTERIM, eff 6-16-96, EXPIRES: 10-14-96; ss and moved by #6337, eff 9-25-96 (from Saf-C 202.07); amd by #7349, eff 8-22-00; amd by #8174, INTERIM, eff 9-25-04, EXPIRES: 3-24-05; ss by #8230-A, eff 12-17-04 (formerly Saf-C 203.04)",
